\name{cellucid_history_saved_open}
\alias{cellucid_history_saved_open}
\title{Open a saved state}
\usage{
cellucid_history_saved_open(viewer, saved)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{saved}{Its id (history_saved_list). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{already_shown} (It is the history shown already, which goes on; nothing was opened), \code{dataset} (The name of its dataset, now open), \code{dataset_opened} (Its dataset was opened first (another one was shown)), \code{name} (Its name; null for an autosave), \code{not_restored} (Null when every part was restored. Otherwise each part that could not be (a state domain such as the Expression values, a tracker's steps), one sentence each, as the person was told: that part is left as it was shown (a part saved by another version of Cellucid that this one cannot read says so), the rest is restored, and the saved state is kept as it was while the history goes on beside it), \code{saved}, \code{steps}.
}
\description{
Open one saved state of this browser (by its id from history_saved_list) to continue it, as Load\ldots's Open does: its dataset first when another is shown (with the cells it was saved on), then its history, which goes on where it left off (an autosave keeps being written; a named save stays as it was and the history goes on as a new autosave). The history shown before stays kept in this browser while Autosave keeps it (steps it does not keep are asked about first). To apply its steps to the dataset shown instead, use history_replay. A whole-file download is asked about first.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.saved.open} (History). It opens another dataset in place of the one the viewer shows, as an agent in the viewer does: it makes no step of the history.

A viewer opened from R shows the dataset R serves, so the viewer refuses this action from R: show another dataset with \code{\link{cellucid_view}}.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (large-download); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_saved_open(viewer, saved = "state-1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
